msgstr "プロジェクトコードはこちらからダウンロードできます。[https://github.com/godotrecipes/3d_car_sphere](https://github.com/godotrecipes/3d_car_sphere)"

#: 3D/3d_sphere_car.md
msgid "In `_physics_process()` we add a force to the body based on the direction the car is pointing, as well as keeping the car mesh positioned at the ball's position:"
msgstr ""
"void _physics_process()\n"
"{\n"
"    // 車の向きに基づいて車体に力を加え、さらに車メッシュをボールの位置に固定します。\n"
"    float3 force = vehicle->GetForwardVector() * kCarForceMagnitude;\n"
"    vehicle->AddForceAtPosition(force, ballPosition);\n"
"\n"
"    // 車メッシュの位置をボールの位置に設定\n"
"    meshComponent->SetLocalTranslation(ballPosition);\n"
"}"

#: 3D/3d_sphere_car.md
msgid "Observe the difference:"
msgstr "違いを観察してください。"

#: 3D/3d_sphere_car.md
msgid "If you've tried driving on a slope, you've seen that the car mesh doesn't tilt at all, it always remains level. That looks unnatural, so let's use the process described in [KinematicBody: Align with Surface](/godot_recipes/3.x/3d/3d_align_surface/) to fix that."
msgstr "坂での走行を試したことがある方ならご存知でしょうが、車オブジェクトは傾斜が全くつかず、常に水平を保っています。これは不自然に見えるため、[KinematicBody: 表面と位置合わせ](/godot_recipes/3.x/3d/3d_align_surface/) セクションで説明されている方法を使って修正しましょう。"

