msgstr "### セットアップ方法"

#: physics/collision_layers.md
msgid "Collision Layers and Masks"
msgstr "衝突レイヤーとマスク"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "This is the node that implements simulated 2D physics. You do not control a rigid body directly, but instead you apply forces to it (gravity, impulses, etc.) and the physics engine calculates the resulting movement. See [Godot 3.0: Rigid Bodies](/blog/2017/12/godot3_kyn_rigidbody1/) for more information."
msgstr "このノードはシミュレーションされた2D物理を実装しています。直接リジッドボディを操作するのではなく、重力やインパルスなどの力を適用することで、物理エンジンがその結果生じる移動量を計算します。詳細は[Godot 3.0: リジッドボディ](/blog/2017/12/godot3_kyn_rigidbody1/)の記事をご覧ください。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/k2d_platf_sample.gif?width=300)"
msgstr "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/k2d_platf_sample.gif?width=300)"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "Using KinematicBody2D"
msgstr "KinematicBody2Dをつかう"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"This happens because there is no _collision response_. `move_and_collide()` just stops\n"
"the body's movement when a collision occurs. We need to code whatever response we\n"
"want from the collision."
msgstr "これは、衝突時の応答処理が定義されていないためです。`move_and_collide()` は単に衝突が発生した時点で物体の動きを停止させます。衝突に対して実装したい特定の応答ロジックをコーディングが必要です。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "In game development you often need to know when two objects in the game space intersect or come into contact. This is known as _collision detection_. When a collision is detected, you typically want something to happen. This is known as _collision response_."
msgstr "ゲーム開発において、ゲーム内空間内の二つのオブジェクトが交差するか接触するかどうかを判断する必要が生じる場面は頻繁に存在します。これは「衝突検知」と呼ばれる処理です。衝突が検出された場合、通常は何らかのアクションを発生させたいものです。この部分を総称して「衝突応答」と呼びます。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"|           |Layers|Mask|\n"
"|-----------|------|----|\n"
"|**Player** |`1`|`2, 3` |\n"
"|**Enemy**  |`2`|`1`    |\n"
"|**Coin**   |`3`|`1`    |"
msgstr ""
"|レイヤー | マスク       |\n"
"|----------------|-------------|\n"
"|     **プレイヤー** | `1` | `2, 3` |\n"
"|     **敵キャラ**   | `2` | `1`    |\n"
"|     **コイン**     | `3` | `1`    |"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func get_input():\n"
"\t# add these actions in Project Settings -> Input Map\n"
"\tvelocity = Vector2()\n"
"\tif Input.is_action_pressed('backward'):\n"
"\t\tvelocity = Vector2(-speed/3, 0).rotated(rotation)\n"
"\tif Input.is_action_pressed('forward'):\n"
"\t\tvelocity = Vector2(speed, 0).rotated(rotation)\n"
"\tif Input.is_action_just_pressed('mouse_click'):\n"
"\t\tshoot()"
msgstr ""
"func get_input():\n"
"\t# add these actions in Project Settings -> Input Map\n"
"\tvelocity = Vector2()\n"
"\tif Input.is_action_pressed('backward'):\n"
"\t\tvelocity = Vector2(-speed/3, 0).rotated(rotation)\n"
"\tif Input.is_action_pressed('forward'):\n"
"\t\tvelocity = Vector2(speed, 0).rotated(rotation)\n"
"\tif Input.is_action_just_pressed('mouse_click'):\n"
"\t\tshoot()"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"{{< highlight python>}}\n"
"var collision = move_and_collide(velocity * delta)\n"
"if collision:\n"
"\tvelocity = velocity.slide(collision.normal)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}\n"
"{{< highlight python>}}\n"
"velocity = move_and_slide(velocity)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}"
msgstr ""
"{{< highlight python>}}\n"
"var collision = move_and_collide(velocity * delta)\n"
"if collision:\n"
"\tvelocity = velocity.slide(collision.normal)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}\n"
"{{< highlight python>}}\n"
"velocity = move_and_slide(velocity)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func change_state(new_state):\n"
"    state = new_state\n"
"    match state:\n"
"        IDLE:\n"
"            new_anim = 'idle'\n"
"        RUN:\n"
"            new_anim = 'run'\n"
"        JUMP:\n"
"            new_anim = 'jump_up'"
msgstr ""
"function change_state(new_state) {\n"
"  state = new_state;\n"
"  switch (state) {\n"
"    case IDLE:\n"
"      new_anim = 'idle';\n"
"      break;\n"
"    case RUN:\n"
"      new_anim = 'run';\n"
"      break;\n"
"    case JUMP:\n"
"      new_anim = 'jump_up';\n"
"      break;\n"
"    default:\n"
"      new_anim = 'unknown';\n"
"  }\n"
"}"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"When using `move_and_slide()` the function returns a vector representing the\n"
"movement that remained after the slide collision occurred. Setting that value back\n"
"to the character's `velocity` allows us to smoothly move up and down slopes. Try\n"
"removing `velocity =` and see what happens if you don't do this."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"A common question from new Godot users is: \"How do you decide which movement function to use?\"\n"
"Often the response is to use `move_and_slide()` because it's \"simpler\", but this is not\n"
"necessarily the case. One way to think of it is that `move_and_slide()` is a special case,\n"
"and `move_and_collide()` is more general. For example, the following two code snippets result in the same collision response:"
msgstr ""
"新規ユーザーからよく寄せられる質問の一つに「どの移動関数を使えばよいか？」というものがあります。\n"
"多くの場合、「よりシンプルだから」という理由から `move_and_slide()` が推奨されますが、必ずしもそうとは限りません。この概念を理解する一つの方法として、`move_and_slide()` は特殊なケースであり、`move_and_collide()` がより一般的なケースであると考えるとよいでしょう。例えば、以下の2つのコードスニペットはいずれも同じ衝突判定結果になります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "var velocity = Vector2()"
msgstr "var velocity = Vector2()"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"The action happens in `_physics_process()`. After using `move_and_collide()` if a\n"
"collision occurs, a `KinematicCollision2D` object is returned (otherwise, the return\n"
"is `Nil`)."
msgstr "この処理は`_physics_process()`関数内で行われます。`move_and_collide()`を使用した後に衝突が発生した場合、`KinematicCollision2D`オブジェクトが返されます（発生しなかった場合は戻り値は`Nil`となります）。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "`floor_max_angle` - default value: `0.785398` (in radians, equivalent to 45 degrees)"
msgstr "`floor_max_angle` - デフォルト値: `0.785398`（ラジアン単位、約45度に相当）"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "This is the maximum number of collisions before the body stops moving. Setting this too low may prevent movement entirely."
msgstr "これは、物体の運動が停止するまでに発生する衝突の最大回数です。設定値を低くしすぎると、そもそも動きが発生しなくなる可能性があります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "> **Note:** In order to detect collisions, at least one `Shape2D` must be assigned to the object."
msgstr "> ※注意：衝突検出を行うには、対象オブジェクトに少なくとも1つの`Shape2D`が割り当てられている必要があります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "This parameter allows you to define what surfaces the engine should consider to be the floor. Setting this lets you use the `is_on_floor()`, `is_on_wall()`, and `is_on_ceiling()` methods to detect what type of surface the body is in contact with. The default value means that all surfaces are considered walls."
msgstr "このパラメータでは、エンジンが床面として認識すべき表面を指定できます。これを設定すると、`is_on_floor()`、`is_on_wall()`、および `is_on_ceiling()` メソッドを使用して、対象オブジェクトがどの種類の表面に接触しているかを検出できるようになります。デフォルト値はすべての表面が壁として扱われることを意味します。"

