msgstr "### 移動とスライド処理"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func get_input():\n"
"    velocity.x = 0\n"
"    var right = Input.is_action_pressed('ui_right')\n"
"    var left = Input.is_action_pressed('ui_left')\n"
"    var jump = Input.is_action_just_pressed('ui_select')"
msgstr ""
"func get_input():\n"
"    velocity.x = 0\n"
"    var right = Input.is_action_pressed('ui_right')\n"
"    var left = Input.is_action_pressed('ui_left')\n"
"    var jump = Input.is_action_just_pressed('ui_select')"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "You have three nodes with the following configuration:"
msgstr "以下の構成で3つのノードがあります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "{{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D` is for implementing bodies that are to be controlled via code. They detect collisions with other bodies when moving, but are not affected by engine physics properties like gravity or friction. While this means that you have to write some code to create their behavior, it also means you have more precise control over how they move and react."
msgstr "{{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D` は、コードによって制御されるボディを実装するためのものです。移動時に他のオブジェクトとの衝突を検出しますが、重力や摩擦といったエンジンの物理特性の影響を受けません。このため、その動作を生成するためにある程度のコーディングが必要となりますが、その一方で、動き方や反応をより精密にコントロールできるという利点があります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "We're using a very rudimentary state machine to handle the transitions between the character's idle, running, and jumping states."
msgstr "現在、キャラクターの待機状態・走行状態・ジャンプ状態間の遷移を管理するため、非常に基本的なステートマシンを使用しています。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"export (PackedScene) var Bullet\n"
"export (int) var speed"
msgstr ""
"エクスポート (packedscene) 変数 Bullet\n"
"エクスポート (int) 変数 speed"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func _physics_process(delta):\n"
"\tvar collision = move_and_collide(velocity * delta)\n"
"\tif collision:\n"
"\t\tvelocity = velocity.bounce(collision.normal)\n"
"\t\tif collision.collider.has_method(\"hit\"):\n"
"\t\t\tcollision.collider.hit()"
msgstr ""
"func _physics_process(delta):\n"
"\tvar collision = move_and_collide(velocity * delta)\n"
"\tif collision:\n"
"\t\tvelocity = velocity.bounce(collision.normal)\n"
"\t\tif collision.collider.has_method(\"hit\"):\n"
"\t\t\tcollision.collider.hit()"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func _physics_process(delta):\n"
"    velocity.y += gravity * delta\n"
"    if state == JUMP:\n"
"        if is_on_floor():\n"
"            change_state(IDLE)\n"
"    velocity = move_and_slide(velocity, Vector2(0, -1))"
msgstr ""
"velocity.y += gravity * delta\n"
"    if state == JUMP:\n"
"        if is_on_floor():\n"
"            change_state(IDLE)\n"
"    velocity = move_and_slide(velocity, Vector2(0, -1))"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"Run the scene again and try moving into the obstacle. You'll see that the {{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D`\n"
"can't penetrate the obstacle. However, try moving into the obstacle at an angle and\n"
"you'll find that the obstacle acts like glue - it feels like the body gets stuck."
msgstr ""
"sceneを再実行し、障害物に向かって移動してみてください。{{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D` が\n"
"障害物を貫通できないことが確認できるでしょう。ただし、斜めに移動して障害物に接触してみると、\n"
"障害物がまるで接着剤のように作用するのを感じるはずです。ボディが貼り付いたような感覚になります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/k2d_layer_example.png?width=300)"
msgstr "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/k2d_layer_example.png?width=300)"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"Also note that we've added `Vector2(0, -1)` as the floor normal. This is a vector\n"
"pointing straight upward. This means that if the character collides with an object\n"
"that has this normal, it will be considered a floor."
msgstr "また、床面の法線ベクトルとして `Vector2(0, -1)` を追加しました。このベクトルは真上を指しています。つまり、キャラクターがこの法線を持つ物体に衝突した場合、それは床と判定されることを意味します。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "Let's look at each of the properties in turn:"
msgstr "各プロパティを順番に確認していきましょう。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"Run this scene and you'll see that `move_and_collide()` works as expected, moving\n"
"the body along the velocity vector. Now let's see what happens when you add\n"
"some obstacles. Add a {{< gd-icon StaticBody2D >}}`StaticBody2D` with a rectangular collision shape. For visibility,\n"
"you can use a sprite, a {{< gd-icon Polygon2D >}}`Polygon2D`, or just turn on \"Visible Collision Shapes\" from\n"
"the \"Debug\" menu."
msgstr "このシーンを実行すると、`move_and_collide()`が想定通りに動作し、ボディが速度ベクトルに沿って移動することを確認できます。では、障害物を追加した場合にどうなるかを見てみましょう。矩形の衝突形状を持つ{{< gd-icon StaticBody2D >}}`StaticBody2D`オブジェクトを追加してください。視認性を高めるには、スプライトを使用するか、{{< gd-icon Polygon2D >}}`Polygon2D`を使用するか、あるいは「デバッグ」メニューから「可視衝突形状」を有効化する方法もあります。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "The `move_and_slide()` method is intended to simplify the collision response in the common case where you want one body to slide along the other. This is especially useful in platformers or top-down games, for example."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"if jump and is_on_floor():\n"
"        change_state(JUMP)\n"
"        velocity.y = jump_speed\n"
"    if right:\n"
"        change_state(RUN)\n"
"        velocity.x += run_speed\n"
"    if left:\n"
"        change_state(RUN)\n"
"        velocity.x -= run_speed\n"
"    $Sprite.flip_h = velocity.x < 0\n"
"    if !right and !left and state == RUN:\n"
"        change_state(IDLE)"
msgstr ""
"if jump and sprite_is_on_the_floor():\n"
"        set_state(JUMP)\n"
"        velocity.y = jump_speed\n"
"    if moving_right:\n"
"        set_state(RUN)\n"
"        velocity.x += run_speed\n"
"    if moving_left:\n"
"        set_state(RUN)\n"
"        velocity.x -= run_speed\n"
"    $Sprite.flip_h = velocity.x < 0\n"
"    if not moving_right and not moving_left and state == RUN:\n"
"        set_state(IDLE)"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"{{< highlight python >}}\n"
"extends KinematicBody2D"
msgstr ""
"{{< highlight python >}}\n"
"extends KinematicBody2D"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "A static body is one that is not moved by the physics engine. It participates in collision detection, but does not move in response to the collision. This type of body is most often used for objects that are part of the environment or that do not need to have any dynamic behavior."
msgstr "静的ボディとは、物理エンジンによって移動されないオブジェクトです。衝突検知には参加しますが、衝突に応じて移動することはありません。このタイプのボディは、環境の一部となるオブジェクトや、動的な挙動を必要としないオブジェクトに最もよく使用されます。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"The Player is controlled by W/S for forward/back and aims using the mouse. Here is\n"
"the code for the Player, using `move_and_slide()`:"
msgstr "プレイヤーはW/Sキーで前進・後退操作し、マウスを使って狙いを定めます。以下にPlayer用のコードを示します（`move_and_slide()`関数を使用しています）："

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "This is the maximum angle before a surface is no longer considered a \"floor\"."
msgstr "これは、表面がもはや「床」として考慮されなくなる最大角度です。"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func _physics_process(delta):\n"
"\tget_input()\n"
"\tvar dir = get_global_mouse_position() - global_position\n"
"\t# Don't move if too close to the mouse pointer\n"
"\tif dir.length() > 5:\n"
"\t\trotation = dir.angle()\n"
"\t\tvelocity = move_and_slide(velocity)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}"
msgstr ""
"func _physics_process(delta):\n"
"\tget_input()\n"
"\tvar dir = get_global_mouse_position() - global_position\n"
"\t# マウスポインタに近すぎる場合は移動させない\n"
"\tif dir.length() > 5:\n"
"\t\trotation = dir.angle()\n"
"\t\tvelocity = move_and_slide(velocity)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}"

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"What if you don't want a sliding collision response? For this example (\"BounceandCollide.tscn\"\n"
"in the sample project), we have a character shooting bullets and we want the bullets to\n"
"bounce off the walls."
msgstr "※スライディング衝突応答を不要とする場合について。このサンプルケース（「BounceandCollide.tscn」 - サンプルプロジェクト収録）では、キャラクターが弾丸を発射し、壁に当たって跳ね返る挙動を実現しています。"

